    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Jessamy Cotter, Harbour Warden of Gradsul, at the Port Authority.</strong> Forty-four. Non-combatant.</p><p>Every outbound hull in Gradsul is entered, inspected if she likes, and signed out under her seal, and she likes to inspect. She is meticulous, humourless and the one official on the waterfront that both guilds have given up trying to buy. She will sign the Kestrel Wife out on the morning of Day 15 without looking up, unless she has been given a reason to look up.</p><p><strong>Holding a tide:</strong> in a hue and cry she can keep every hull in the harbour at her moorings until the Watch has searched it. She does it perhaps twice a year, and the waterfront talks of nothing else for a week. See <em>Payoff &amp; Consequences</em> in the Gull's Job.</p><p><em>Sheet derived from the Councilman Ortwell Brane stat block (CR 1/2, 31 hp) \u2014 kit renamed and redescribed.</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
